            </li>
          </ul>
          <div
            class="MuiCard-root MuiPaper-elevation MuiPaper-elevation3 MuiPaper-root MuiPaper-rounded css-XXXX-MuiPaper-root-MuiCard-root getting-started__card"
            id="welcome"
          >
            <div
              class="MuiCardContent-root css-XXXX-MuiCardContent-root"
            >
              <h2
                class="MuiTypography-h2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
              >
                Welcome to GraphKB
              </h2>
              <p
                class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
              >
                If you are a new User there are a couple things to do to get started. You will need to sign the end user license agreement in the terms Card 
                <a
                  data-discover="true"
                  href="/about/terms"
                >
                  here
                </a>
                . Once you have signed, you will be able to query GraphKB using this interface of the API. Next you should read through the sections below.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="MuiCard-root MuiPaper-elevation MuiPaper-elevation3 MuiPaper-root MuiPaper-rounded css-XXXX-MuiPaper-root-MuiCard-root getting-started__card"
            id="core-concepts"
          >
            <h2
              class="MuiTypography-h2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Core Concepts
            </h2>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              There are 3 main data types in GraphKB: Statements, Ontologies, and Variants.
            </p>
            <h3
              class="MuiTypography-h3 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Statements
            </h3>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Statements are used to represent the interpretive content or assertions. Statements make up most of the interpretive content of GraphKB. Statements are decomposed sentences which link conditions to a conclusion. There are four main elements to a statement
            </p>
            <img
              alt="Statement Schema"
              src="https://graphkbdev-api.bcgsc.ca/public/pori-statement-schema.svg"
            />
            <ul
              class="MuiList-padding MuiList-root css-XXXX-MuiList-root"
            >
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    Subject
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    This is the element which the relevance of the statement applies to
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    Relevance
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    This adds meaning to a statement and applies to the previous element
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    Conditions
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    This is the statement context. It is a series of required conditions for the statement to be applicable/true
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    Evidence
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    One or more pieces of evidence (Literature, DB, etc) which support this statement
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <h3
              class="MuiTypography-h3 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Variants
            </h3>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Variants can be the well known small mutations (KRAS:p.G12D), fusions, signature variants, expression variants, copy variants, etc. Variant Records are composed of three key attributes: reference1, reference2, and type. All of these are foreign keys to an ontology record. Most often reference1/2 are genes and type is a Vocabulary record.
            </p>
            <img
              alt="Variant Schema"
              src="https://graphkbdev-api.bcgsc.ca/public/pori-positional-variant-schema.svg"
            />
            <ul
              class="MuiList-padding MuiList-root css-XXXX-MuiList-root"
            >
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    reference1
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    the reference element this variant is defined with respect to. Most often a gene
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    reference2
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    reference2 is only used for fusions and structural variants
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    type
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    This is the class this variant belongs to (ex. indel)
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <h3
              class="MuiTypography-h3 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Ontology Terms
            </h3>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Ontologies can be used to represent any set of controlled vocabulary. Important features of an ontology record in GraphKB are
            </p>
            <img
              alt="Ontology Schema"
              src="https://graphkbdev-api.bcgsc.ca/public/pori-ontology-schema.svg"
            />
            <ul
              class="MuiList-padding MuiList-root css-XXXX-MuiList-root"
            >
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    source
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    This is the database or external collection that defines this record (ex. PubMed)
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    sourceId
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    This is the ID for this record as defined by its source definition (ex. PMID:1234). This is essential for tracibility or records
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    name
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    The name is generally the longer form and more human readable form to represent this record. However it can be the same as the sourceId when no other name has been attributed
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    description
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    The definition of the ontology term
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div
            class="MuiCard-root MuiPaper-elevation MuiPaper-elevation3 MuiPaper-root MuiPaper-rounded css-XXXX-MuiPaper-root-MuiCard-root getting-started__card"
            id="statement-examples"
          >
            <h2
              class="MuiTypography-h2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Statement Examples
            </h2>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-paragraph MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Somtimes it can be confusing how to decompose the content you want to enter into a statement. There are recurring type of statements being entered, we will go through examples of some of these types in detail below.
            </p>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-paragraph MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Before a statement can be entered, all of the elements of the statement must first exist so that they can be linked to. In most cases the required elements (variants, therapies, vocabulary, etc.) will already exist. However if they do not, they should be created prior to attempting to input the statement.
            </p>
            <h3
              class="MuiTypography-h3 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Eligibility for a Clinical Trial
            </h3>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              For this example we are attempting to input the following. There is a clinical trial with the trial id NCT0444444 (Fictional trial ID). This trial requires participants to have mutations in the gene EGFR for Eligibility. It also requires the patients to be diagnosed with Lung Adenocarcinoma. Decomposed this becomes
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    subject
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    NCT0444444: Here 'Eligibility' applies to the clinical trial 'NCT0444444'
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    Relevance
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    Eligibility: The purpose or relevance of this statement is 'Eligibility'. This is what we are trying to communicate
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    conditions
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    Lung Adenocarcinoma, and EGFR mutation: These are the conditions required
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <div
                  class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                >
                  <span
                    class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    evidence
                  </span>
                  <p
                    class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                  >
                    NCT0444444: Here the support is also the clinical trial since it is responsible for defining the eligibility requirements
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </p>
          </div>
          <div
            class="MuiCard-root MuiPaper-elevation MuiPaper-elevation3 MuiPaper-root MuiPaper-rounded css-XXXX-MuiPaper-root-MuiCard-root getting-started__card"
            id="querying"
          >
            <h2
              class="MuiTypography-h2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
              id="about-page__querying"
            >
              Querying
            </h2>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-paragraph MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              There are 2 ways to query GraphKB. The basic/quick search is found on the home page of the application and the search Icon will lead users to the advanced search option For more
            </p>
            <ul
              class="MuiList-padding MuiList-root css-XXXX-MuiList-root search-list"
            >
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <a
                  data-discover="true"
                  href="/query"
                >
                  <div
                    class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                  >
                    <span
                      class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                    >
                      Basic/Quick Search
                    </span>
                  </div>
                </a>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <p
                  class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                >
                  This is the simplest way to query. It is the main page view of this application and contains a single text box for input
                </p>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <a
                  data-discover="true"
                  href="/query-advanced"
                >
                  <div
                    class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                  >
                    <span
                      class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                    >
                      Advanced Search
                    </span>
                  </div>
                </a>
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <p
                  class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                >
                  This view is for advanced users and lets the user build their own queries from scratch
                </p>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <h3
              class="MuiTypography-h3 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
              id="about-results-table"
            >
              Viewing Results (Table)
            </h3>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              After sending a query, result records will be loaded into the Table view
            </p>
            <img
              alt="Query Results"
              id="query-table-view"
              src="/src/static/images/table-view.png"
            />
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-paragraph MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Clicking any row in table view will open the details panel. From the details panel you can view or edit the record in a new window
            </p>
            <h4
              class="MuiTypography-h4 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Configuring Table Options
            </h4>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-paragraph MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Clicking the top-right ellipsis to modify the visible columns or export the current table to a document
            </p>
          </div>
          <div
            class="MuiCard-root MuiPaper-elevation MuiPaper-elevation3 MuiPaper-root MuiPaper-rounded css-XXXX-MuiPaper-root-MuiCard-root getting-started__card"
            id="adding-data"
          >
            <h2
              class="MuiTypography-h2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
              id="about-forms"
            >
              GraphKB Forms
            </h2>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-paragraph MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              When filling out forms, certain fields will behave differently from others based on the type of input. The following are several of the core field types that you will encounter when interacting with GraphKB through this GUI:
            </p>
            <h3
              class="MuiTypography-h3 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              List Fields
            </h3>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-paragraph MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              List fields are used for properties that are lists of strings. To use these, simply type the item you wish to add to the list, and press enter or click the add button to add it to the list. Items can be deleted by backspacing against them or clicking the
              <q>
                x
              </q>
               shown in the example image.
            </p>
            <img
              alt="List Fields"
              src="/src/static/images/list-fields.png"
            />
            <h3
              class="MuiTypography-h3 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Link Fields
            </h3>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-paragraph MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Some records in GraphKB are dependent on or reference others. To express these links in forms, a small query bar is included to allow you to find the linked record you need. Start typing and wait for the dropdown list of items to appear for you to pick from. The default query logic is to match the record
              <q>
                name
              </q>
               property. If you require more control over finding this linked record, some link fields have an expand button that creates a mini-form to fill out, similar to the Advanced Query form. You can clear the existing linked record by clicking the
              <q>
                x
              </q>
               as shown in the example image.
            </p>
            <ul
              class="MuiList-padding MuiList-root css-XXXX-MuiList-root"
            >
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root about-page__image-list css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <h4
                  class="MuiTypography-h4 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                >
                  Before Input
                </h4>
                <img
                  alt="blank link field"
                  src="/src/static/images/single-autocomplete-1.png"
                />
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root about-page__image-list css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <h4
                  class="MuiTypography-h4 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                >
                  Auto-completion on Type
                </h4>
                <img
                  alt="searching link field"
                  src="/src/static/images/single-autocomplete-2.png"
                />
              </li>
              <li
                class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root about-page__image-list css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
              >
                <h4
                  class="MuiTypography-h4 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                >
                  Selected Input
                </h4>
                <img
                  alt="selected link field"
                  src="/src/static/images/single-autocomplete-3.png"
                />
              </li>
            </ul>
            <h3
              class="MuiTypography-h3 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Select Fields
            </h3>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-paragraph MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              Select fields are used to select an item from a set of options. Most selects are able to be set to a null/empty value, but for mandatory selects an option must be chosen before submitting the form.
            </p>
            <img
              alt="Select Fields"
              src="/src/static/images/select-fields.png"
            />
          </div>
          <div
            class="MuiCard-root MuiPaper-elevation MuiPaper-elevation3 MuiPaper-root MuiPaper-rounded css-XXXX-MuiPaper-root-MuiCard-root getting-started__card"
            id="graph-view"
          >
            <h2
              class="MuiTypography-h2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
              id="about-results-graph"
            >
              Graph View
            </h2>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              The Graph view can be used to view clusters of records and their relationships with eachother. Click and drag nodes with your mouse or finger, and open the Graph settings to change labels, coloring schemes, and physical behavior of the graph and its constituents.
            </p>
            <img
              alt="Graph"
              src="/src/static/images/graph-view.png"
            />
            <h3
              class="MuiTypography-h3 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
              id="about-results-graph"
            >
              Graph Node Actions
            </h3>
            <p
              class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
            >
              After clicking a graph node or link, you will see this actions ring appear, which will allow you to
            </p>
            <div
              class="about-page__column-image"
            >
              <img
                alt="Graph Node Actions"
                src="/src/static/images/graph-actions.png"
              />
              <p
                class="MuiTypography-body1 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
              >
                <ul
                  class="MuiList-padding MuiList-root css-XXXX-MuiList-root"
                >
                  <li
                    class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
                  >
                    <div
                      class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                    >
                      <span
                        class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                      >
                        Expand
                      </span>
                      <p
                        class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                      >
                        Expand the record to view its related records
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                  <li
                    class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
                  >
                    <div
                      class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                    >
                      <span
                        class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                      >
                        Hide
                      </span>
                      <p
                        class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                      >
                        Hide the record from the graph
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                  <li
                    class="MuiListItem-dense MuiListItem-gutters MuiListItem-padding MuiListItem-root css-XXXX-MuiListItem-root"
                  >
                    <div
                      class="MuiListItemText-dense MuiListItemText-multiline MuiListItemText-root css-XXXX-MuiListItemText-root"
                    >
                      <span
                        class="MuiListItemText-primary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                      >
                        Details
                      </span>
                      <p
                        class="MuiListItemText-secondary MuiTypography-body2 MuiTypography-root css-XXXX-MuiTypography-root"
                      >
                        View record details in a side drawer
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
`;

